From: Kuzma30 <kuzemkoa@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:28:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] Modeling Algorithms - Count only the surfdatas of the
 end edge at the end of a fillet

FreeCAD issue 20085, a cube of 20 with fillets of radius 6 and a square
hole of 8 x 8 whose walls go along the tangent lines of the fillets of
the cube. A vertical (concave) edge of the hole and the two upper edges
at it are filleted (Fillet001), then a lower edge next to that vertical
edge (Fillet002). The spine of the second fillet goes on along the edge
of the first one at the bottom of the hole and along the next lower edge:
the fillet goes round the corner of the hole, crossing several faces
there. The result had a volume of 4872 mm3 instead of 5150 and a
tolerance of 9.5.

ChFi3d_Builder::PerformIntersectionAtEnd compared the number of
surfdatas of the stripe with the number of edges of its spine: when they
differ, the last surfdata was taken for a short piece across smooth
edges at the end, and the end was closed by PerformMoreThreeCorner when
an edge next to the spine at the vertex was smooth (here the edge between
the fillet of the cube and its sphere). The surfdatas are now counted on
the edge of the spine at the vertex only: with one surfdata there, the
end is computed as for a fillet of one edge (the end in the plane of the
next wall of the hole).

The second fillet is valid for r = 0.5 to 2 after the vertical edge alone
(tolerance 1.4e-4 to 4.9e-4) or with the upper or the lower edges at it
(the tolerance of the corner of the first fillets); each lower or upper
edge next to the vertical one was tried.

New DRAW test bugs/modalg_8/fillet_rounded_cube_square_hole_rim_after_corner
and GTest
BRepFilletAPI_MakeFilletTest.SquareHoleInRoundedCube_RimFilletGoesRoundFilletedCorner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01N85duF92anuCHYJzUxLgPg
